! Periodic Hirshfeld atom refinement (pHAR) of ammonium closo-hexaborane(6),
! against a CRYSTAL23 periodic wavefunction. Rescued 2026-08-16 from
! archive/release-pHAR-broken (Kanghyun Chu, 2025-04-29, tip 18712bd6).
!
! WHY THIS TEST MATTERS: pHAR ships in the library and, until now, NOTHING
! tested it. MOLECULE.CE:phar_defragment is live, and crystal.foo,
! molecule.har.foo and molecule.rho.foo all carry pHAR-specific branches.
!
! ================================================================
! THIS TEST IS SKIPPED UNLESS YOU FETCH A 167 MB FILE FIRST:
!
!     scripts/fetch_phar_asset.sh
!
! ================================================================
!
! WHY THE FILE IS NOT COMMITTED. GenerateXML.XML is the CRYSTAL23 periodic
! wavefunction, 174,978,609 bytes. Committing it -- or committing its Git LFS
! pointer together with a .gitattributes that tracks it -- makes EVERY clone of
! this repository pull 167 MB, because LFS smudges the checked-out ref
! automatically for anyone who has git-lfs installed. GitHub's free allowance is
! 1 GB of storage AND 1 GB/month of bandwidth, so a handful of clones exhausts
! it. For one test, in a public repository, that is a bad trade.
!
! So `develop` and `master` carry NO LFS objects at all -- verify with
! `git lfs ls-files develop`, which must print nothing. The asset lives only on
! the tag archive/release-pHAR-broken, and the fetch script pulls it from there.
! Keep it that way: do NOT add a .gitattributes tracking *.XML, and do NOT
! commit the pointer here. That is precisely the mistake this arrangement
! exists to avoid.
!
! If the LFS object is ever pruned, Crystal23_InputFiles.zip (12 KB, committed)
! is what regenerates the XML -- that is why 18712bd6 added it. Needs CRYSTAL23.
!
! ONE EDIT WAS MADE TO THE ORIGINAL JOB, and it is a port not a workaround. As
! committed on the branch it died with
!
!     unknown option: thermal_smearing_model=
!
! That keyword was removed by acb7af0b, "Removed 'temperature_factor_model' and
! a few others, in favour of deriving the info from partition_model". The job
! already sets partition_model= oc-crystal23, which now carries that
! information, so the line was deleted.
!
! REFERENCE. Re-blessed 2026-08-16 from a current build, because the 2025-04
! reference echoed the removed keyword and contained a "Form factor asymmetry"
! section this build no longer prints. The NUMBERS were unchanged -- the rescued
! job reproduces the 2025-04 reference digit for digit:
!
!     Structure fit converged.
!     R(F)   0.005188      N_r 20      N_p 11
!     GoF^2  0.631422      GoF 0.794621     scale 0.979852
!
! Runtime about 3 m 40 s, the slowest test in the suite -- hence label "long".

   input : B6H6_grown.cif
   input : tonto_data_on_F_20rfl.hkl
   input : GenerateXML.XML

   delete: stderr

